uld be  in the original dooms beta known as The  BFG 2704 in the doom Bible which is what  the original games design document was  known as the edge rereads BFG 2704 red  horrible hallway scouring weapon damages  user a bit or for recoil BFG stands for  big and gun safest use back to wall  distant target the BFG fired a rapid  stream of green and red plasma  projectiles which could bounce around  the environment continuing to do damage  to the demons caught in their wake  however with a number of sprites on  screen the weapon could cause the game  to slow down and according to John  Romero the red and green plasma sprites  looked a bit too Christmasy so the  design was scrapped in favor of the big  green energy blasts we now associate  with the BFG 9000  [Music]  when dreamers released in 1993 the  earliest players could get their hands  on the weapon was in a third mission of  the third episode pandemonium being the  last and most powerful firearm that doom  guy could bring to bear it was  understandably saved for the latter  parts of the game where cyber demons and  spite of masterminds demand more  ordnance to dispose off in Doom - the  weapon remained unchanged instead simply  continuing its legacy of reducing  enemies to a crimson paste and while The  BFG received a facelift three years  later in Doom 64 it still retained the  course cyberdemon melting power the  weapon was known for well you know what  they say if you're glowing green  superweapon ain't broke don't fix it it  wasn't until June 3 when we really got a  new version of The BFG to play with for  this version there were some changes  from previous titles like having  separate ammunition rather than being  forced to share rounds of the plasma  rifle and having a charged option for a  more powerful shot  in my opinion the best thing it did for  Doom 3 was bring the game back to its  old-school sheet of roots doom 3 felt  more like a horror game than a shooter  it was dark at jump scares and forced  you to ditch weapons in order to hold a  flashlight and the whole experience was  much more slow and deliberate than what  Doom was known for that is however until  you got to the final act of the game  where both demons and ammunition was  plentiful your arsenal was overflowing  and you could let loose with much more  reckless abandon than you could in  previous hours of playing that was where  the game felt like dooms of old and that  was where the BFG was most at home big  hordes of demons disappearing under a  green glow at the pull of a trigger the  appearance of The BFG 9000 in doom 2016  however is still a moment that fills me  with excitement and an urge to rip and  tear even four years later this is a  game encapsulate the energy of Doom and  wears it proudly on its sleeve as soon  as you get through to the highly secured  BFG you're immediately thrown into a  situation for you to make the most of  its destructive power a room full of  enemies to Jib as the hammering tones of  Mick Gordon's BFG division begin to  pound through your speakers  [Music]  it is a moment that distills the BFGS  legacy in a concentrated stream of  intensity motion and simulated violence  it's with this reason that I would  revert to checkpoint and replay the  moment again and again it's satisfying  and rewarding on so many levels as a  technically impressive set piece a story  beats and as a moment to really engage  that primal part of your brain that  takes so much enjoyment in seeing stuff  blow up the first time I played through  this section I didn't realize that my  heart was so high or that I was holding  in such a deep breath until I heard the  soothing tones of a computerized voice  echo while I think we all knew that the  BFG 9000 would return and doom eternal  it wasn't until III 2019 that we got our  first glimpse at its famous green glow  as its span up against a cyberdemon in  an utter tease as the screen cuts to  black before the shot is unleashed in  the lead-up to eternal is also the first  time we got to see the real in universe  successor to the big gun in the form of  the Phobos planetary cannon The BFG  10,000  the legacy of The BFG though cannot be  contained to the hellscape doom it  became an icon when the FPS genre was  still in its formative years where  dozens of doom clones attempted to  replicate the visceral experience  through their own settings and weapons  and would continue to appear in other in  software game 1997's quake 2 featured a  nod to the weapon with its own BFG 10k  which works in a similar way to the doom  versions quake 3 had a weapon with the  same name but instead shoots a  rapid-fire explosive projectiles similar  to Jim's plasma rifle is present in the  bizarre 2005 mobile game doom RPG in the  doom tabletop game is an action car that  can even all all defense and dodges in  the dream comic our green marine hero  actually weeps when he acquires it but I  was hired as June fans wept during its  appearance in the terrible doom movie as  the bio force gun version 3.1 for  [Music]  Caudill a terrible name  2011 s rage introduced a weapon called  the authority pulse cannon  whose secondary fire used in alternate  ammunition type called pfg rounds and it  even appeared in 2019 s rage to where  you could find a familiar facsimile the  weapon assuming you have the special  addition to game and had synced up your  professor account now one of the reasons  this weapon is so legendary is down to  the sheer number of times has been  referenced in movies TV shows video  games and even beyond honestly the only  way I'm gonna get through them is if I  rattle them off rapid fire mode the 2004  PC RPG sacred had an attack called BFG  Ratchet and Clank up your arsenal had a  level called the nefarious BFG a 2005  criterion software shoot of black  references the m249 machine gun as the  BFG globally popular mobile league of  legends has an item named the BF sword  although not to be outdone blizzards own  MOBA hair as the storm has a character  named sergeant hammer whose ultimate  ability is the blunt force gun indie  roguelike and the gungeon has a weapon  known as the BSG leg shoot a gun that  acts like the BFG 9000 half-life  opposing force is a weapon called the  displacer cannon that seemingly works in  the same way as the BFG it was a Magic  the Gathering expansion pack in 1998  that featured a B F M or big furry  monster a creature that was so big it  took up two cards the largest can of the  energy drink monks  that used to be able to buy was called  the B F scene according to an interview  with GQ Elon Musk's internal names for  the space X's and Mars Rockets are known  as the PFR and the BFS big rocket and  big in spaceship  it's amazing to think that the BFG 9000  has become such an iconic weapon within  games considering where it came from  this simple toy gun went on to inspire  one of the most revered virtual  artifacts in gaming history now did the  original it team think that the design  would become such an impactful source of  inspiration and parody I don't think  they're plans with that grandiose in  fact I think the simplest explanation is  the most likely that they just wanted to  make a big [ __ ] gun thank you so much  for watching our little love letter to  the BFG 9000 if you enjoyed make sure  you like the video leave your thoughts  in the comment section down below and if  you new here make sure you go back and  watch the other episodes of loadout  there are already on our YouTube channel

